BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Building LLM Inference Services for Researchers on HPC with Open O
 nDemand - Heechang Na [Ohio Supercomputer Center]
DTSTART;TZID=US/Mountain:20260310T113000
DTEND;TZID=US/Mountain:20260310T115500
DTSTAMP:20261020T211022Z
UID:pretalx-good-2026-AWC8QJ@pretalx.com
DESCRIPTION:We share how we built LLM inference services for researchers a
 t Ohio Supercomputer Center (OSC) using Open OnDemand. Our users need LLMs
  in many different ways\, so we support several service models. We started
  with an Ollama module on the cluster\, added OpenWebUI\, and later create
 d dedicated OnDemand apps that start the LLM server and give users a simpl
 e interface. We also provide a Jupyter + Ollama app that exposes an OpenAI
  API interface in a Jupyter kernel. We maintain shared models so users can
  start quickly\, while still allowing local models. We have also deployed 
 the Ollama + OpenWebUI service on our Kubernetes cluster\, but scaling it 
 for a large number of users remains a challenge. We plan to add additional
  LLM engines and front-ends as part of our future improvements as well.
LOCATION:Main Hall
URL:https://pretalx.com/good-2026/talk/AWC8QJ/
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
